# Shopify `productSet` push rules

## Non-negotiable payload rule

When **`productSet.variants`** includes **`optionValues`**, the payload **MUST** also include non-empty **`productOptions`** (default single-option kit shape: `Title` / `Default Title`).

This applies to **create and update**, including **partial bulk push** (quantities-only, price-only, etc.).

- Enforced in code: `ShopifyProductSetPayloadValidator::assertValid()` (called before every GraphQL `productSet` write).
- Do **not** omit `productOptions` on update paths to “send fewer fields”.

## Required tests before finishing Shopify push work

Run and keep green:

1. `php artisan test --filter=ShopifyProductSetPayloadValidator`
2. `php artisan test --filter=ShopifyProductUpsertFromErpService`
3. `php artisan test --filter=PushSelectedProductToShopifyJob`

Must include the **Products bulk-push default matrix** (user workflow):

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| info | true |
| images | **false** (tunnel often off) |
| quantities | true |
| price | true |
| publish_status | true |
| sales_channels | true |

Assert the recorded `productSet` has **`productOptions`**, variant **`id`**, and expected partial/full fields.

## Queue worker after PHP write changes

Bulk push runs on **`pricing-tool-queue`**. After changing Shopify write services/jobs:

```powershell
docker exec pricing-tool-php php artisan queue:restart
```

Long-running `queue:work` may serve stale OPcache until restarted — code on disk is not enough.

